    <innernamespace refid="namespaceanonymous__namespace_02passwordcrypt_8cpp_03">anonymous_namespace{passwordcrypt.cpp}</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>The implementation of the password hashing and checking wrapper. (Originally: &quot;Implementation for passwordcrypt: Ensures libsodium is
initialized before any hashing or verification.&quot;). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file sets up libsodium once, turns a plain password into a self-describing Argon2id hash, and checks plain passwords against stored hashes. It understands both the new Argon2id format and the older scrypt format so old accounts are not locked out.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is where the actual password cryptography happens. The session manager calls these functions (through <ref refid="classPasswordWorker" kindref="compound">PasswordWorker</ref>) during login and logout. If this code were missing, the server could not safely store passwords or prove that a supplied password is correct, so authentication would be impossible.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>libsodium password hashing API: <ulink url="https://doc.libsodium.org/password_hashing/">https://doc.libsodium.org/password_hashing/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Argon2id explained: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argon2">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argon2</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>scrypt explained: <ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrypt">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrypt</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>OWASP password storage advice: <ulink url="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html">https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::optional: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
